      "title": "B - small + warped: classic vs ArUco",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "B) Detector robustness. The code is shrunk to ~100 px and perspective-warped (BORDER_CONSTANT white - BORDER_DEFAULT would mirror the code into the empty canvas). At that size the CLASSIC scanline detector no longer finds the finder patterns (empty text, found = false), while the ARUCO-BASED detector still locates and reads it.\n\n'CV QR Decode At Points' closes the loop: hand the classic DECODER the quad the ArUco detector found and it reads the payload fine - detection and decoding stay composable, so any quad source (contour quad, homography, annotated points) can feed the decoder.\n\nTry: drag the destination quad in 'warped quad (small + skewed)' outwards - once the code is big enough the classic detector finds it too."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
