      "title": "A - encode / decode round trip",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "QR codes with OpenCV's OWN objdetect implementation - no model files, unlike 'CV WeChat QR Detect' (workflow 37, cv2.dnn).\n\nA) Round trip: 'CV QR Encode' (cv2.QRCodeEncoder) writes the code, 'CV QR Detect' (cv2.QRCodeDetector) reads it back. 'straight_codes' is the rectified, binarized symbol the decoder actually read - preview it to see what the detector saw. Every knob is a named dropdown: error correction level, encoding mode, version (symbol size).\n\nTry: raise 'version' to make the symbol bigger, drop 'module_size' to 1 to see the raw bitmap, or type a longer payload and watch the auto-picked version grow (the 'version' output reports it)."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
