      "title": "C - Structured Append (one message, three codes)",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "C) Structured Append. 'structure_number' = 3 splits one long message over three codes; the encoder emits them as an IMAGE BATCH. A decoder only reassembles the message when it sees ALL the parts in ONE image, so the batch is tiled vertically ('Image Batch -> CV Batch' + 'CV Reshape Array': a (3, H, W, 3) batch reshaped to (3*H, W, 3) IS the vertical concatenation - the parts are equal-sized and each carries its own quiet zone).\n\nThe detector then reports 3 codes and writes the WHOLE joined message on the first one; the other two decode to empty strings.\n\nTry: raise 'structure_number' to 4 (and set cols on the reshape node to the new frame width) or delete one part and watch the message disappear."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
