      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "D - error correction level vs damage",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "D) What the error-correction level buys. The SAME payload is encoded at level L (~7% recovery) and level H (~30%), then both get the same 90x90 red patch stamped over their middle (cv2.rectangle, thickness -1 = filled).\n\nThe L code stops DECODING - the detector still locates the symbol, but the payload is unrecoverable, so 'text' comes out empty. The H code still reads: that redundancy is why H is the level to use for codes that get printed, scratched, or have a logo pasted on them. It costs symbol size: same text, 296 px at L vs 360 px at H.\n\nTry: shrink the patch (rec_w / rec_h) until L recovers, or grow it until H gives up."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
